WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:05.000
On Monday the 23rd of May 1994, a violent storm hit the city of Perth, Western Australia. Peter Lawrence was at home with one of his daughters. He was concerned. It was getting late and his wife, Pamela Lawrence, hadn't gotten home from work yet. He called her store at 6.15pm. When he didn't get an answer, he decided he had better go down and check on her. Andrew Mallard was born on the 16th of August 1962. His parents were Roy and Grace Mallard.
1994年5月23日星期一，一场猛烈的风暴袭击了西澳大利亚州的珀斯市。彼得·劳伦斯当时正和他的一个女儿在家。他很担心，因为天色已晚，他的妻子帕梅拉·劳伦斯还没下班回家。他在下午6点15分给她的店打了电话。当无人接听时，他决定最好亲自去看看她。安德鲁·马拉德出生于1962年8月16日。他的父母是罗伊和格蕾丝·马拉德。

2
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:50.000
Andrew was born in England where his father Roy had a long career in the army. The Mallards were a hardworking, well respected and law-abiding family. Andrew also had an older sister, Jackie, who was 10 years older than him. The Mallards left England in 1967 and moved to Perth in Western Australia. Andrew had difficulty fitting into his new country. He was exceptionally tall for his age and that, combined with his English accent, was good enough to make him a target for bullies. Kids would mimic his accent, call him lots of colourful names and someone as far as to attack him physically. Andrew never felt like he belonged.
安德鲁出生在英国，他的父亲罗伊在军队中有着长期的职业生涯。马拉德一家勤劳、受人尊敬且守法。安德鲁还有一个比他大10岁的姐姐杰基。马拉德一家于1967年离开英国，搬到了西澳大利亚州的珀斯。安德鲁很难融入这个新国家。他比同龄人高出许多，再加上他的英国口音，这足以让他成为霸凌的目标。孩子们会模仿他的口音，给他起各种难听的外号，甚至有人对他进行身体攻击。安德鲁从未感到自己属于这里。

3
00:01:50.000 --> 00:02:25.000
High school was even worse. Andrew being the type of kid that bullies could feel safe in hitting because they knew he wouldn't hit back. Andrew left school at 16 with no plans or career path in mind. When he turned 18, Andrew started hitting the nightclub scene. He was now a six foot, six inch tall adult. He definitely stood out in the crowd. It was the nightclub scene that introduced him to marijuana and he was soon smoking it regularly. His parents didn't approve of where Andrew was heading in life.
高中生活更糟糕。安德鲁属于那种霸凌者觉得打他很安全的孩子，因为他们知道他不会还手。安德鲁16岁时辍学，没有计划，也没有职业方向。18岁时，安德鲁开始混迹夜店。他现在是一个身高6英尺6英寸的成年人，在人群中非常显眼。正是夜店生活让他接触到了大麻，并很快开始定期吸食。他的父母并不赞同安德鲁的人生方向。

4
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:59.000
He was broke, unemployed and living at home. So he decided to do something he thought would impress them. He enlisted in the army. But he wasn't cut out for it. He never made it through basic training, instead being offered a medical discharge due to a mild sleeping disorder. Andrew returned back to Perth and got back to his old nightclubbing and dope smoking ways. He felt lost in life without a purpose. Convinced he didn't belong in Australia, he pestered his parents to buy him an airfare back to England.
他身无分文、失业且住在家里。于是他决定做一件他认为能让他们印象深刻的事：他参了军。但他并不适合军队。他没能通过基础训练，反而因为轻微的睡眠障碍被医疗退伍。安德鲁回到珀斯，又回到了他以前混夜店和吸毒的老路。他感到迷茫，生活失去了目标。他确信自己不属于澳大利亚，于是缠着父母给他买回英国的机票。

5
00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:37.000
But he didn't do much good over there either. And it wasn't long before his parents were paying for an airfare to get him back home to Perth. By this stage, Andrew was on the verge of a complete breakdown. He couldn't go outside because he started suffering from extreme anxiety and panic attacks. His father Roy sent him to a psychologist who he met with every week for a few months. It really helped him start to get back on track. Andrew stopped smoking pot and he felt like he was ready to move out and face the world again. He moved into a shared accommodation place in South Perth.
但他在那边也没什么长进。没过多久，他的父母又不得不掏钱买机票让他回珀斯。到了这个阶段，安德鲁处于彻底崩溃的边缘。他不敢出门，因为他开始遭受极度的焦虑和恐慌发作。他的父亲罗伊送他去看心理医生，他每周去见一次，持续了几个月。这确实帮助他开始重回正轨。安德鲁停止了吸食大麻，他觉得准备好搬出去重新面对世界了。他搬进了南珀斯的一处合租房。

6
00:03:37.000 --> 00:04:15.000
But his newfound optimism was short-lived when he was unsuccessful at a number of job interviews. When one of his housemates lit up a joint, Andrew couldn't resist his old habit. Within a few months he was broken homeless, wandering in the streets of Perth. In May 1994, Andrew met a girl named Michelle. He was instantly attracted to her. The feeling wasn't mutual, but Michelle did allow Andrew to sleep on her lounge. He couldn't believe his luck. An attractive woman was taking him in.
但他新获得的乐观情绪并没有持续多久，因为他在几次求职面试中都失败了。当他的一个室友点燃一支大麻烟时，安德鲁没能抵挡住旧习。几个月内，他就变得身无分文、无家可归，在珀斯的街头流浪。1994年5月，安德鲁遇到了一个叫米歇尔的女孩。他立刻被她吸引了。这种感觉并非双向的，但米歇尔确实允许安德鲁睡在她的沙发上。他简直不敢相信自己的运气，一位迷人的女性收留了他。

7
00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:48.000
She lived in a flat just off Glide Street in Mosman Park. It took less than a week for Andrew to outstay his welcome note. Whenever Michelle started hinting it might be time for him to move on, Andrew did whatever he could to find her some marijuana. Michelle loved the smoke, and when she was stoned, the talk about him moving out stopped. Michelle didn't even know Andrew's real name. She believed Andrew was an English backpacker named Andre, who just needed somewhere to crash while he waited for some money to be transferred from England.
她住在莫斯曼公园格莱德街附近的一间公寓里。不到一周，安德鲁就招人嫌了。每当米歇尔暗示他该搬走时，安德鲁就会想尽办法为她找大麻。米歇尔喜欢抽大麻，当她吸嗨了之后，关于让他搬走的话题就停止了。米歇尔甚至不知道安德鲁的真名。她以为安德鲁是一个叫安德烈的英国背包客，只是在等待从英国转账过来的钱期间需要个落脚点。

8
00:04:48.000 --> 00:05:20.000
That story didn't last long because Michelle found a copy of his resume in his backpack. But Andrew wasn't about to tell his real story. He said he was really an agent from Interpol, working to break an organised crime syndicate in Fremantle. His real name was Michael Faraday. The resume for Andrew Mallard was part of his cover. Apparently Michelle bought the story. Andrew was in the middle of a manic episode. He was spiraling out of control.
那个故事没持续多久，因为米歇尔在他的背包里发现了一份他的简历。但安德鲁并不打算说出真相。他说他其实是国际刑警组织的特工，正在努力破获弗里曼特尔的一个有组织犯罪集团。他的真名是迈克尔·法拉第。安德鲁·马拉德的简历是他掩护身份的一部分。显然，米歇尔相信了这个故事。安德鲁正处于躁狂发作期，他正在失控。

9
00:05:20.000 --> 00:06:09.000
He had been coming under the attention of local police due to his ever-increasing erratic behaviour. But on the night of Sunday the 22nd of May 1994, he took things up a notch. Andrew left Michelle's place and went to a nearby unit block where a former boyfriend of Michelle's lived. He started bashing down the door of the caretaker's unit, demanding that the caretaker let him into the unit of the old boyfriend. His story? He was a drug squad detective and he had just received information that were drugs stashed in his unit. When the caretaker told Andrew she didn't have a key, he broke down his door. He was actually there to look for some items that Michelle claimed her old boyfriend had stolen from her.
由于他日益古怪的行为，他已经引起了当地警方的注意。但在1994年5月22日星期日晚上，他变本加厉了。安德鲁离开米歇尔的住处，去了附近的一个单元楼，那里住着米歇尔的前男友。他开始猛砸管理员的房门，要求管理员让他进入前男友的单元。他的借口是：他是缉毒组的侦探，刚收到消息说那个单元里藏有毒品。当管理员告诉安德鲁她没有钥匙时，他撞开了门。他其实是去寻找米歇尔声称被前男友偷走的物品。

10
00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:54.000
He was basically just trying to impress her. Andrew didn't find the stolen items in his unit, but he did steal his guitar and a few jackets. But it didn't take long for the old boyfriend to put it all together, and very soon the police came looking for Andrew. He was arrested the next day, Monday the 23rd of May 1994. While he was back at the police station, he was left unattended at a desk for a period of time. So he helped himself to a police type in and a badge. He thought those would come in handy to help sell his story to Michelle and impress her even more. He was at the station until about 3.45pm when he was released.
他基本上只是想给她留下深刻印象。安德鲁没有在那个单元里找到被盗物品，但他确实偷走了他的吉他和几件夹克。但没过多久，前男友就拼凑出了真相，很快警察就来找安德鲁了。他于第二天，即1994年5月23日星期一被捕。当他在警察局时，有一段时间被独自留在桌子旁。于是他顺手拿走了一个警用打字机和一个徽章。他认为这些东西能派上用场，帮他向米歇尔兜售他的故事，让她更崇拜他。他在下午3点45分左右被释放。

11
00:06:54.000 --> 00:07:30.000
He waited around for a while before eventually finding a taxi. He jumped in and instructed the driver to head to Mosman Park. He got there around 5pm. On that afternoon, Perth was hit by a massive freak storm. There were gale force winds, lightning, thunder and heavy rain. The type of storm that knocked down power poles and blacked out traffic lights. Pamela Lawrence was working in her jewellery store called Flora Metallica. It wasn't a traditional type of jewellery store.
他在附近徘徊了一会儿，最终打到了一辆出租车。他跳上车，指示司机前往莫斯曼公园。他在下午5点左右到达那里。那天下午，珀斯遭遇了一场巨大的异常风暴。狂风、闪电、雷鸣和大雨。这种风暴吹倒了电线杆，导致交通信号灯熄灭。帕梅拉·劳伦斯正在她的珠宝店“金属植物群”（Flora Metallica）工作。那不是一家传统的珠宝店。

12
00:07:30.000 --> 00:08:19.000
Pam liked to dip everyday items into various metals and create her own unique style of jewellery. Her shop was located in the Glide Street shopping area in Mosman Park, near Michelle's unit. Pam was a theatre nurse before deciding on the career change. She had been lovingly married to Peter Lawrence for 23 years and they had two daughters, Amy and Katie. Pam was a friendly, bubbly person who could light up a room. Mosman Park is a mostly affluent suburb of Perth, 11km or roughly 5 miles south west of the CBD. With the Indian Ocean to the west and the Swan River to the east, it has its fair share of greened, expensive houses and well-to-do residents.
帕姆喜欢将日常用品浸入各种金属中，创造出她自己独特的珠宝风格。她的店位于莫斯曼公园的格莱德街购物区，靠近米歇尔的公寓。帕姆在决定转行前是一名手术室护士。她与彼得·劳伦斯恩爱地结婚了23年，他们有两个女儿，艾米和凯蒂。帕姆是一个友好、活泼的人，能点亮整个房间。莫斯曼公园是珀斯一个主要富裕的郊区，位于中央商务区西南11公里（约5英里）处。西临印度洋，东临天鹅河，这里有许多绿树成荫的昂贵住宅和富裕的居民。

13
00:08:19.000 --> 00:09:05.000
Although it did have its share of government housing units where a lot of the residents were less desirable types, most were unemployed and addicted to drugs, turning to crime to fuel their habits. The shops around Glide Street had been the targets of several recent break-ins. Flora Metallica hadn't been broken into, but somebody had thrown a brick through the front window. The recent criminal activity led Pam to instruct her staff members that if anyone broke in or tried to rob them while they were there, just to hand over whatever they wanted. Money and material objects weren't worth getting hurt over. Pam did have a staff member working with her that day, Jackie Barsden, but she finished at 3pm.
虽然这里也有一些政府住房单元，很多居民属于不太受欢迎的类型，大多数人失业并沉迷于毒品，通过犯罪来维持他们的瘾。格莱德街周围的商店最近多次成为入室盗窃的目标。“金属植物群”没有被盗过，但有人曾向店门前的窗户扔过砖头。最近的犯罪活动导致帕姆指示她的员工，如果有人闯入或试图在他们上班时抢劫，直接交出他们想要的东西即可。金钱和物质不值得为此受伤。帕姆那天确实有一名员工和她一起工作，杰基·巴斯登，但她在下午3点就下班了。

14
00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:50.000
After that, Pam was by herself. Still on that same afternoon, the 23rd of May, 13-year-old Catherine Barsden had been picked up from school by her grandmother. Catherine, the daughter of Jackie Barsden, who worked at Flora Metallica with Pam. In order to get home, Catherine's grandmother had to drive directly past the store. They actually got stopped at traffic lights directly outside. Catherine got a shock when she looked inside the shop from the car and saw a strange Caucasian man standing behind the counter. She described him as being 30-35 years old, medium-billed, a slight orange beard, 6 feet tall,
那之后，帕姆就独自一人了。还是在5月23日那天下午，13岁的凯瑟琳·巴斯登被她的祖母从学校接走。凯瑟琳是和帕姆一起在“金属植物群”工作的杰基·巴斯登的女儿。为了回家，凯瑟琳的祖母必须开车直接经过那家店。他们实际上在店外的交通灯处停了下来。凯瑟琳从车里往店里看时，看到一个陌生的白人男子站在柜台后面，这让她大吃一惊。她描述他大约30-35岁，中等身材，留着淡淡的橙色胡须，身高6英尺，

15
00:09:50.000 --> 00:10:23.000
and it looked like he was wearing a bandana. Catherine kept staring at the man, and he eventually made eye contact with her, after which he immediately crouched down behind the counter. Catherine had never seen the man in the shop before. She thought it was strange and made sure to look at the clock in the car. The time was two minutes past five. She told her mum Jackie when she got home. Jackie thought it sounded strange, so she picked up the phone to call Pam to make sure she was okay.
看起来像是戴着头巾。凯瑟琳一直盯着那个男人看，他最终与她有了眼神接触，之后他立即蹲到了柜台后面。凯瑟琳以前从未在店里见过这个男人。她觉得这很奇怪，并特意看了看车里的时钟。时间是5点02分。她回家后告诉了她的妈妈杰基。杰基觉得这听起来很奇怪，于是拿起电话打给帕姆，想确认她是否平安。

16
00:10:23.000 --> 00:11:02.000
But then she changed her mind, deciding it was probably nothing. Peter Lawrence was at home with one of his daughters. He was concerned that his wife, Pam, hadn't returned home from work yet. He called the store at quarter past six to see when she planned on getting home. When Pam didn't answer, he decided he had better go down and check on her. At 6.39pm, a call was made to emergency services. A woman had been attacked. An ambulance was requested to the Flora Metallica Jewelry Store at Mosman Park.
但随后她改变了主意，觉得可能没什么事。彼得·劳伦斯当时正和他的一个女儿在家。他担心妻子帕姆还没下班回家。他在6点15分给店里打了电话，想看看她打算什么时候回家。当帕姆没有接听时，他决定最好亲自去看看她。下午6点39分，有人拨打了紧急服务电话。一名女子遭到袭击。救护车被要求前往莫斯曼公园的“金属植物群”珠宝店。

17
00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:33.000
Peter Lawrence had walked into the store to find Pam lying in a pool of blood with severe head wounds. Peter was covered in blood himself as he was kneeling down next to his wife, trying to help her when the ambulance and police arrived. Pam had lost leaders of blood. She was barely breathing. They put her on a stretcher and rushed her to hospital. On the way to the hospital, her breathing stopped. They performed CPR and did everything they could, but it was too late.
彼得·劳伦斯走进店里，发现帕姆躺在血泊中，头部受了重伤。当救护车和警察到达时，彼得跪在妻子身边试图帮助她，他自己也浑身是血。帕姆流了很多血，几乎没有呼吸了。他们把她抬上担架，紧急送往医院。在去医院的路上，她的呼吸停止了。他们进行了心肺复苏术，尽了一切努力，但已经太晚了。

18
00:11:33.000 --> 00:12:08.000
Pam was dead on arrival. A later autopsy would reveal that Pam died as a result of her severe head wounds. The cause of the wounds was an unknown blunt force object. There were no defensive injuries. In Pam's wounds, the forensic pathologist found little specs of an unknown blue material. It was believed that that material came from the murder weapon. Detectives from the major crime squad were called in. The lead detective of the investigation was Detective Sergeant Sherville,
帕姆在到达医院时已经死亡。后来的尸检显示，帕姆死于严重的头部创伤。伤口的原因是某种未知的钝器。没有防御性伤口。在帕姆的伤口中，法医病理学家发现了少量未知的蓝色物质。人们认为该物质来自凶器。重案组的侦探被召集起来。调查的首席侦探是谢维尔警长，

19
00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:52.000
assisted by Detective Caporn and a whole team of other detectives. Little was done that night in the way of a forensic investigation. The Jewelry Store was locked and guarded until the following day when a thorough examination could take place. A search was conducted to try and find the murder weapon, but they turned up nothing. Peter Lawrence pointed out that no money had been stolen from the register and no jewelry had been taken. But Pam's purse was missing. It was the next day, Tuesday the 24th of May, when police first learned about the suspicious man Catherine Barstyn had seen in the store. There was other information to consider too.
在卡彭侦探和整个侦探团队的协助下。那天晚上在法医调查方面做得很少。珠宝店被锁上并守卫着，直到第二天进行彻底检查。警方进行了搜查以试图找到凶器，但一无所获。彼得·劳伦斯指出，收银机里没有钱被偷，也没有珠宝被拿走。但帕姆的钱包不见了。第二天，即5月24日星期二，警方才第一次了解到凯瑟琳·巴斯登在店里看到的那个可疑男子。还有其他信息需要考虑。

20
00:12:52.000 --> 00:13:37.000
Reports that unknown people were seen in the area acting suspiciously around the time of the murder. Other reports of some of the known local junkies hanging around too. And what about some of the undesirable characters that live in the government housing flats nearby? Or the mental health patient that lives there? Maybe it's related to the break-ins, or the brick that was thrown through the window of the store not that long ago. Many names were added to a list of possible suspects, but none of them were very solid at that stage. The list ended up containing over a hundred names. The main concern for detectives was finding out who the suspicious man in the store was that Catherine Barstyn had seen.
有报告称在谋杀发生时，有人看到不明身份的人在附近行为可疑。还有其他关于一些已知的当地瘾君子在附近游荡的报告。住在附近政府住房公寓里的那些不受欢迎的角色呢？或者住在那里的一名心理健康患者？也许这与入室盗窃有关，或者与不久前扔进店窗户的那块砖头有关。许多名字被列入嫌疑人名单，但在那个阶段，没有一个是非常确凿的。名单最终包含了100多个名字。侦探们的主要关注点是找出凯瑟琳·巴斯登在店里看到的那个可疑男子是谁。

21
00:13:37.000 --> 00:14:25.000
An identity keep drawing was made up of the man based on Catherine's description and it was sent out to the media. The forensic pathologist concluded that 5pm when she saw the man fit the time frame of the attack as PM could have remained alive that long. Naturally, Peter Lawrence was a suspect in his wife's murder. But there was nothing to cast suspicion on Peter other than the fact he found his wife's body. There were no reports of violence or any other issues in the house. They were still very much in love. His daughters had no doubt that he was innocent. It was Thursday, three days after the murder, when the name of 31-year-old Andrew Mallard was first mentioned to police.
根据凯瑟琳的描述，制作了一张该男子的身份拼图，并发送给了媒体。法医病理学家得出结论，她看到该男子的5点钟符合袭击的时间框架，因为帕姆可能在那之前一直活着。自然，彼得·劳伦斯是妻子谋杀案的嫌疑人。但除了他发现了妻子的尸体外，没有任何证据让彼得受到怀疑。没有关于家中暴力或其他问题的报告。他们仍然非常相爱。他的女儿们毫不怀疑他是无辜的。那是谋杀发生三天后的星期四，31岁的安德鲁·马拉德的名字第一次被提到给警方。

22
00:14:25.000 --> 00:15:20.000
As part of the investigation, police did an extensive door knock of surrounding residents. One of the people they spoke to was Michelle, the girl who had let Andrew sleep on her lounge. It was Detective Caporn who spoke with her and he learned all about Michelle's strange housemate with his weird stories and unpredictable erratic behaviour. He had been arrested for the break-in on the morning of the murder and she was sure he didn't get home until about 6.30pm on that night. Andrew wasn't home to be questioned though. He had already attended court for the break-in charge and the judge recommended that he be sent to Greyland Psychiatric Hospital for a 28-day mental health assessment. That got Detective Caporn even more interested. Caporn went to the hospital to speak to Andrew.
作为调查的一部分，警方对周围居民进行了广泛的走访。他们交谈的人之一是米歇尔，那个让安德鲁睡在沙发上的女孩。是卡彭侦探与她交谈的，他了解到了米歇尔那个奇怪的室友，以及他那些古怪的故事和不可预测的反复无常的行为。他在谋杀当天早上因入室盗窃被捕，她确信他那天晚上直到6点30分左右才回家。不过安德鲁不在家接受询问。他已经因入室盗窃指控出庭，法官建议将他送往格雷兰精神病院进行28天的心理健康评估。这让卡彭侦探更加感兴趣。卡彭去医院找安德鲁谈话。

23
00:15:20.000 --> 00:16:21.000
He thought to himself that he sort of looked like the authentic picture that was made of the man Catherine Baslin saw in the store. He let Andrew know he was investigating the murder of Pamela Lawrence and asked where he was at the time of the murder. Andrew let Caporn know that after he got released from the police station, he called a taxi back to Michelle's unit in Mosman Park, getting him there around 5pm. That didn't fit with what Caporn had been told by Michelle. She said it was more like 6.30pm when he got home. Caporn also found out that Andrew used to wear bandanas, although he said he stopped wearing them several months earlier. Caporn then paid a visit to the taxi company. He found the driver who picked up Andrew. The driver didn't have any trouble remembering him because he said he was a rock star from England. He said he didn't drop him off at Michelle's unit block. It was a completely different unit block.
他心想，他看起来有点像凯瑟琳·巴斯登在店里看到的那个男人的拼图。他让安德鲁知道他正在调查帕梅拉·劳伦斯的谋杀案，并询问他在谋杀发生时在哪里。安德鲁告诉卡彭，他从警察局获释后，打了一辆出租车回到米歇尔在莫斯曼公园的单元，大约下午5点到达那里。这与卡彭从米歇尔那里得到的消息不符。她说他回家时更像是6点30分。卡彭还发现安德鲁过去常戴头巾，尽管他说几个月前就不戴了。卡彭随后拜访了出租车公司。他找到了载安德鲁的司机。司机对他记忆犹新，因为他说他是来自英国的摇滚明星。他说他没有把他送到米歇尔的单元楼，而是完全不同的一个单元楼。

24
00:16:21.000 --> 00:17:18.000
Nearby, but definitely not Michelle's. Andrew told the driver he was just going in to get some friends and he would be right back. It was 5pm, but Andrew never returned. By 20 past 5, the driver realized he had done the runner on him. Caporn returned back to the hospital the next day, eager to question Andrew about this new information. He wanted to know more about this missing 90 minutes between 5pm when he got out of the taxi and 6.30pm when Michelle says he got home. It was during this second chat that Andrew came clean. He admitted running off without paying for the taxi and he says he got dropped off at that particular unit block because he knew people who he could escort to. Andrew gave numerous names of people he was with or spoke to.
就在附近，但绝对不是米歇尔的。安德鲁告诉司机他只是进去找几个朋友，马上就回来。当时是5点，但安德鲁再也没有回来。到5点20分，司机意识到他逃单了。卡彭第二天回到医院，急于就这一新信息询问安德鲁。他想更多地了解下午5点他下出租车到下午6点30分米歇尔说他回家之间缺失的90分钟。正是在第二次谈话中，安德鲁坦白了。他承认没付车费就跑了，并说他被送到那个特定的单元楼是因为他认识可以投靠的人。安德鲁提供了他与之在一起或交谈过的许多人的名字。

25
00:17:18.000 --> 00:18:22.000
Detectives canvassed the unit block trying to verify his story, but they couldn't. No one remembered being with Andrew during that time. Caporn got a warrant and took Andrew's clothing for forensic testing. His right shoe tested positive for two different blood groups. One was undetermined. The second was from Blood Group B, the same blood group of Pamela Lawrence that was found in only 4% of the population. Inconsistent stories, no alibi, an admitted drug user who was displaying such bizarre behavior that it led him to being sent to a psychiatric hospital on a court order. And now there was the blood. Caporn was convinced he had his man. He briefed the rest of the detectives on the case what he had uncovered. And on Friday the 3rd of June the full result of the DNA test was revealed. The moment Caporn had been waiting for.
侦探们走访了那个单元楼试图核实他的故事，但没能做到。没有人记得在那段时间和安德鲁在一起。卡彭拿到了搜查令，取走了安德鲁的衣服进行法医鉴定。他的右鞋检测出两种不同的血型。一种未确定。第二种是B型血，这是帕梅拉·劳伦斯的血型，仅存在于4%的人口中。前后矛盾的故事，没有不在场证明，一个承认吸毒的人，表现出如此怪异的行为，以至于被法院命令送往精神病院。现在还有了血迹。卡彭确信他抓住了凶手。他向案件的其他侦探通报了他所发现的情况。6月3日星期五，DNA测试的全部结果公布了。卡彭一直在等待这一刻。

26
00:18:22.000 --> 00:19:10.000
Was it Pamela's blood on Andrew's shoe? No. The initial tests were incorrect. It was actually Andrew's blood. It was the following Friday the 10th of June 94 that Andrew was released from hospital. He was diagnosed with manic depression and bipolar disorder, but he didn't have to stay there any longer. His condition was manageable so long as he agreed to keep regular appointments for treatment. Andrew had to reappear before a judge, who ruled that he was officially free to go. Detective Caporn was waiting for him in the courtroom. He approached Andrew and asked if he was prepared to go back to the station and answer a few more questions.
安德鲁鞋上的血是帕梅拉的吗？不是。最初的测试是不正确的。那实际上是安德鲁自己的血。6月10日星期五，安德鲁从医院获释。他被诊断出患有躁狂抑郁症和双相情感障碍，但他不必再待在那里了。只要他同意定期预约治疗，他的病情是可以控制的。安德鲁必须再次出庭，法官裁定他正式获释。卡彭侦探在法庭上等着他。他走近安德鲁，问他是否准备好回到警察局再回答几个问题。

27
00:19:10.000 --> 00:20:01.000
If he agreed Caporn would give him his clothes and shoes back. Once they got to the police station they went straight into an interview room. They went back over Andrew's story, what he did and where he was on the day of Pamela's murder. Andrew gave the same version. He was released from the police station, caught a taxi, did the runner, tried to buy some marijuana, then returned to Michelle's flat. He also informed Caporn that he had been inside Flora Metallica in the days before the murder. He was trying to sell some of his jewellery, but he was told they weren't that type of store. Andrew wasn't under arrest. Officially he was there of his own free will. Having a chat and to get his clothes back. So his rights weren't read to him.
如果他同意，卡彭会把他的衣服和鞋子还给他。他们一到警察局就直接进了审讯室。他们重新梳理了安德鲁的故事，他在帕梅拉谋杀当天做了什么，在哪里。安德鲁给出了相同的版本。他从警察局获释，打了一辆出租车，逃了单，试图买些大麻，然后回到米歇尔的公寓。他还告诉卡彭，他在谋杀前几天曾进入过“金属植物群”。他试图卖掉他的一些珠宝，但被告知他们不是那种店。安德鲁没有被捕。正式来说，他是自愿在那里的。聊聊天，拿回他的衣服。所以没有向他宣读权利。

28
00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:54.000
They started poking holes in his story about the missing 90 minutes. Andrew would give a name of someone who we thought he had spoken to in that time and the detectives would knock it down. Sorry we spoke to him and it was actually Sunday the night before the murder that you were together. How come you can't remember where you were or what you were doing Andrew? Why are you lying Andrew? What are you trying to hide Andrew? Just make it easier on yourself. Tell us the truth. What really happened? We can help you. The detectives also knew about the type in and police badge Andrew had stolen to impress Michelle. When asked about those items, he said a friend had given them to him. But they had serial numbers. The detectives knew he was lying.
他们开始在他关于缺失90分钟的故事中寻找漏洞。安德鲁会说出一个他认为在那段时间里交谈过的人的名字，侦探们就会推翻它。“抱歉，我们和他谈过了，你们在一起实际上是谋杀前一天的星期日。安德鲁，你怎么会不记得你在哪里或在做什么？安德鲁，你为什么要撒谎？安德鲁，你想隐瞒什么？让自己轻松点吧。告诉我们真相。到底发生了什么？我们可以帮你。”侦探们也知道安德鲁为了给米歇尔留下深刻印象而偷走的打字机和警察徽章。当被问及这些物品时，他说是一个朋友给他的。但它们有序列号。侦探们知道他在撒谎。

29
00:20:54.000 --> 00:21:54.000
After about six or seven hours into the interview, Andrew started giving an account. Like a hypothetical account. What he believed happened. As if he was a psychic. Saying that he could get into the killer's head and read his mind. And see what happened. He started saying he thought the person responsible was evil and scared. And he just kept hitting Pam and couldn't stop. This got Caporn's attention. He read Andrew his rights. Andrew continued giving his theory. I think he was just looking to steal something. He went in through the back door. She was still in the shop locking up and saw him. He got scared. So he kept on hitting her and couldn't stop. He hit her on the head repeatedly with a wrench. Then he saw the girl in the car looking at him. He got scared and had to get out.
审讯进行了大约六七个小时后，安德鲁开始给出一个陈述。就像一个假设的陈述。他认为发生了什么。就好像他是一个通灵者。说他可以进入凶手的头脑，读懂他的心思。并看到发生了什么。他开始说他认为负责的人是邪恶和害怕的。他只是不停地打帕姆，无法停止。这引起了卡彭的注意。他向安德鲁宣读了他的权利。安德鲁继续给出他的理论。“我想他只是想偷点东西。他从后门进去。她还在店里锁门，看到了他。他害怕了。所以他不停地打她，无法停止。他用扳手反复击打她的头部。然后他看到车里的女孩在看着他。他害怕了，必须离开。”

30
00:21:54.000 --> 00:22:56.000
So he moved the body, dragged her to the back door. She was making gurgling noises. So he hit her again. Then ran out. Where was the wrench the detectives asked? Andrew said the killer caught a train to North Fremantle and threw it in the ocean. Andrew was trying to please the detectives and tell them what they wanted to hear so he could get out of the interview room. Caporn took Andrew's third person account as a confession. When the detectives wanted to go back through his story again and get to the bottom of how he knew all that information if he didn't do it. Andrew lost it and started yelling and swearing, denying he was responsible, protesting his innocence. Andrew's aggression led to a physical altercation and he ended up biting Caporn. The interview was over. They charged him with assaulting a police officer but he wasn't held in custody. He was released.
“所以他移动了尸体，把她拖到后门。她发出咕噜声。所以他又打了她。然后跑了。”侦探们问扳手在哪里？安德鲁说凶手坐火车去了北弗里曼特尔，把它扔进了海里。安德鲁试图取悦侦探，告诉他们他们想听的话，这样他就能离开审讯室。卡彭把安德鲁的第三人称陈述当作了供词。当侦探们想再次梳理他的故事，并弄清楚如果不是他做的，他怎么知道所有这些信息时。安德鲁崩溃了，开始大喊大叫和咒骂，否认他负责，抗议他的清白。安德鲁的攻击性导致了身体冲突，他最终咬了卡彭。审讯结束了。他们指控他袭击警察，但他没有被拘留。他被释放了。

31
00:22:56.000 --> 00:23:48.000
He never got his clothes or shoes back though. None of that first interview was recorded. The detectives made notes of what was said but they weren't signed by Andrew. While that interview was being conducted, Peter Lawrence was on the phone to Detective Sherville. He told him that he thought a 10-inch Sidcrome wrench was missing from out the back of PM's jewellery shop. The reason Andrew was allowed to go was so they could run an undercover operation on him. They didn't have enough evidence. They didn't have any evidence really. All they had was Andrew's unrecorded ramblings of a third person account of how he thought the murder happened. They needed more. So Andrew was about to meet a new friend.
但他再也没拿回他的衣服或鞋子。第一次审讯的内容都没有录音。侦探们记录了所说的话，但安德鲁没有签字。在进行那次审讯时，彼得·劳伦斯正在给谢维尔侦探打电话。他告诉他，他认为帕姆珠宝店后面少了一把10英寸的Sidcrome扳手。安德鲁被允许离开的原因是他们可以对他进行卧底行动。他们没有足够的证据。他们实际上没有任何证据。他们所拥有的只是安德鲁关于他认为谋杀是如何发生的第三人称的未录音的胡言乱语。他们需要更多。所以安德鲁即将结识一位新朋友。

32
00:23:48.000 --> 00:24:35.000
They were hoping he would confess and lead the undercover officer to the murder weapon and to PM's purse. Andrew had nowhere to go. Michelle wasn't having him back and he didn't want to go back home to his parents. So he was forced to sleep in a park. It was only a few days later while Andrew was hanging in the park that he met Gary. He instantly hit it off with Gary and was impressed when he drove him around to score some dope. He was even more impressed when Gary shouted him a couple of nights in a hotel room. Gary said he was writing a book on PMler's murder and he wanted Andrew's help. Gary wanted to know all about Andrew's theory of what happened.
他们希望他能坦白，并引导卧底警官找到凶器和帕姆的钱包。安德鲁无处可去。米歇尔不让他回去，他也不想回家找父母。所以他被迫睡在公园里。仅仅几天后，当安德鲁在公园里闲逛时，他遇到了加里。他立刻和加里合得来，当他开车带他去买毒品时，他印象深刻。当加里请他在酒店住几晚时，他印象更深了。加里说他正在写一本关于帕姆·劳伦斯谋杀案的书，他需要安德鲁的帮助。加里想知道关于安德鲁对所发生事情的理论的一切。

33
00:24:35.000 --> 00:25:17.000
