所以安德鲁给了他与给侦探们讲的相同的故事。加里随后开始提到武器，并想知道安德鲁的想法。加里甚至提到了扳手，特别提到了Sidcrome扳手。他问安德鲁他怎么想。那可能是凶器吗？他还问他是否认为会有很多血。凶手会怎么处理他的衣服，凶手会从哪里得到武器，凶手会把武器扔在哪里。安德鲁非常乐意推测。根据安德鲁的回答，加里的报告后来写道，谋杀的动机是抢劫。

34
00:25:17.000 --> 00:26:05.000
The murder weapon was a wrench. The wrench had been thrown off a bridge into the Swan River and the killer washed the blood off his clothes using the salt water in the river. In Andrew's words, that would fuck with the forensics. Again, Andrew hadn't confessed directly, but the police believed what he was saying was information only the killer would know and he was giving his confession in some sort of speculative third-person way. Andrew wasn't well. Between their in-depth discussions about Pam's murder, he was smoking a heap of pot and his behaviour was getting more erratic. He started talking about how he had passed through several dimensions and his soul could enter different bodies.
凶器是一把扳手。扳手被从桥上扔进了天鹅河，凶手用河里的盐水洗掉了衣服上的血迹。用安德鲁的话说，那会“搞乱法医”。同样，安德鲁没有直接坦白，但警方认为他所说的是只有凶手才知道的信息，他正在以某种推测性的第三人称方式进行供述。安德鲁身体不好。在他们关于帕姆谋杀案的深入讨论之间，他抽了大量大麻，他的行为变得越来越古怪。他开始谈论他是如何穿过几个维度的，他的灵魂可以进入不同的身体。

35
00:26:05.000 --> 00:26:47.000
He also mentioned that he was really a Viking warrior. That comment led Gary to encourage Andrew to participate in a makeover. Gary bought him a pair of boots, an army jacket and a kilt at a second-hand store. Then he took him to get his head partly shaved. There you go, Andrew. You look much more like a Viking warrior now. Gary started to fear for his safety, believing Andrew was a murderer and seeing his behaviour get more and more erratic. The undercover operation was called off. No admissions were made and they never got led to the murder weapon or to Pam's purse.
他还提到他其实是一名维京战士。那个评论促使加里鼓励安德鲁参加一次大改造。加里在一家二手店给他买了一双靴子、一件军用夹克和一条苏格兰短裙。然后带他去把头剃了一部分。“给你，安德鲁。你现在看起来更像一名维京战士了。”加里开始担心自己的安全，认为安德鲁是一名杀手，并看到他的行为变得越来越古怪。卧底行动被取消了。没有做出任何承认，他们也从未被引导找到凶器或帕姆的钱包。

36
00:26:47.000 --> 00:27:28.000
Andrew failed to attend court for the assault police charge, so a warrant was issued for his arrest. He was arrested by Detective Brandon, who was also working on Pam's case. He was taken back to the police station and put back into the same interview room that he was in before. Detective Brandon wanted him to answer some more questions about Pam's murder. Andrew went back to his third-person theories about what he thought had happened. This time he added in a description of Pam's injuries. Andrew was able to describe them because he says he was shown a photo of them in the first interview. They handed Andrew a piece of paper.
安德鲁未能就袭击警察的指控出庭，因此发出了逮捕令。他被也在调查帕姆案件的布兰登侦探逮捕。他被带回警察局，放回了他之前所在的同一个审讯室。布兰登侦探想让他回答更多关于帕姆谋杀案的问题。安德鲁回到了他关于他认为发生了什么的第三人称理论。这一次他加入了一段对帕姆伤口的描述。安德鲁能够描述它们，因为他说他在第一次审讯中被展示了一张照片。他们递给安德鲁一张纸。

37
00:27:28.000 --> 00:28:38.000
They told him to draw the wrench that he believes the killer used. Andrew did as he was told. He even wrote the word SIGCHROME on the wrench, remembering what Gary had told him. Andrew was interviewed for over 11 hours this second time round, of which only 30 minutes was recorded on video. A record of the rest of the interview was completed by the detectives making unsigned notes, just like the first interview. When the tape was turned on, they went back over the story, now asking him questions based on all the information Andrew had given them, mostly in the third person. But he also spoke in the first person at times. We brought you in this morning and we had a conversation in relation to the murder of Pam Lawrence at Mosman Park.
他们告诉他画出他认为凶手使用的扳手。安德鲁照做了。他甚至在扳手上写下了“SIGCHROME”这个词，记住了加里告诉他的话。安德鲁第二次被审讯了超过11个小时，其中只有30分钟被录像。其余审讯的记录由侦探们完成，他们做了未签名的笔记，就像第一次审讯一样。当录音带打开时，他们重新梳理了故事，现在根据安德鲁给他们的所有信息问他问题，大多是第三人称。但有时他也用第一人称说话。“我们今天早上把你带进来，我们进行了关于帕姆·劳伦斯在莫斯曼公园被谋杀的谈话。”

38
00:28:38.000 --> 00:29:05.000
Do you agree with that? I do. During the course of those discussions, he told us certain things. You said that you needed money. I did. And you told us that you went in through the rear of the shop at Flora Metallica. Is that what you told us? I told you that.
“你同意吗？”“我同意。”“在这些讨论过程中，你告诉了我们某些事情。你说你需要钱。”“我说了。”“你告诉我们你从‘金属植物群’商店的后部进去。这是你告诉我们的吗？”“我告诉过你。”

39
00:29:05.000 --> 00:29:30.000
I'm just going to go through that now. What you told us? We'll sort the rest out later. You told us that you went on the front on Glow Street and that you were looking back and you saw that the Flora Metallica, the door was shut. And that you thought that it was closed so it was safe to do a break. Is that what you told us? Okay. You described the steps to us and you described the rear door and the fly screen door.
“我现在要梳理一下。你告诉我们的？剩下的我们以后再处理。你告诉我们你去了格莱德街的前面，你回头看，你看到‘金属植物群’，门关着。你认为它关了，所以入室盗窃是安全的。这是你告诉我们的吗？”“好的。”“你向我们描述了台阶，你描述了后门和纱门。”

40
